{"timestamp":"2026-05-26T23:27:51.979Z","ordinal":42,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_1gMoPFMsMBJnEhh4RMIanLcZ","output":"Chunk ID: febb36\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1274\nOutput:\n307\n00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,492\nWhat were her notes?\n\n308\n00:21:24,575 --> 00:21:25,951\nShe hates them.\n\n309\n00:21:26,035 --> 00:21:27,036\nOh.\n\n310\n00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,667\nWhat about recreating\nthe Heart-Shaped Herb?\n\n311\n00:21:33,751 --> 00:21:35,961\nHave you made\nany progress on that?\n\n312\n00:21:36,045 --> 00:21:37,254\nGRIOT: Excuse me, Princess.\n\n313\n00:21:37,338 --> 00:21:40,549\nNakia, daughter of Yaa,\nis trying to reach you again.\n\n314\n00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:41,634\nMaybe you should...\n\n315\n00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:43,469\nMaybe you should\ncontinue your calculations\n\n316\n00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:44,720\nas I instructed.\n\n317\n00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,305\nGRIOT: As you wish, Princess.\n\n318\n00:21:47,807 --> 00:21:49,350\nWe do not need the Herb,\nMother.\n\n319\n00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,394\nWe need new technology.\n\n320\n00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:53,729\nWhat of the Black Panther?\n\n321\n00:21:56,941 --> 00:22:00,611\nThe mantle has unified\nour nation for centuries.\n\n322\n00:22:00,694 --> 00:22:02,863\nThe Black Panther\nis a relic, Mother.\n\n323\n00:22:02,947 --> 00:22:05,449\nI wasn't trying to save\nthe mantle with the Herb,\n\n324\n00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,701\nI was trying\nto save my brother.\n\n325\n00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,163\nRAMONDA: Oh, Shuri.\n\n326\n00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,040\n(SIGHS)\n\n327\n00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:20,339\n(SIGHS)\n\n328\n00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:26,679\nDo you know what day it is?\n\n329\n00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,763\nTuesday.\n\n330\n00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,558\nThe date, child.\n\n331\n00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:33,686\n(SHURI SIGHS)\n\n332\n00:22:36,814 --> 00:22:38,065\nBrother's passing.\n\n333\n00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,025\nOne year ago today.\n\n334\n00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,245\nHave you planned anything?\n\n335\n00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:55,249\nYes. It involves you taking\nyour mother for a drive.\n\n336\n00:22:55,833 --> 00:22:57,251\n-Right now?\n-Right now.\n\n337\n00:22:57,918 --> 00:22:59,545\nAnd you can leave\nyour Kimoyo Beads here.\n\n338\n00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:00,754\n-Mother.\n-No, no.\n\n339\n00:23:00,838 --> 00:23:02,673\nYou won't need them\nwhere we are going.\n\n340\n00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:05,426\nHmm?\n\n341\n00:23:07,428 --> 00:23:10,389\nAnd the other two. Yes.\n\n342\n00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:12,266\n(SHURI SCOFFS)\n\n343\n00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:24,028\n(DISTANT ANIMAL CALLS)\n\n344\n00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:28,782\n(SIGHS)\n\n345\n00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,245\n(INSECTS CHIRPING)\n\n346\n00:23:34,163 --> 00:23:38,000\nYou need to sit here with me.\nAnd with yourself.\n\n347\n00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,669\nIt is the only way\nyou are going to heal\n\n348\n00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:43,088\nfrom the wound caused\nby T'Challa's death.\n\n349\n00:23:43,172 --> 00:23:44,465\nI'm fine, Mother.\n\n350\n00:23:45,883 --> 00:23:47,843\nYou don't have to worry\nabout me.\n\n351\n00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:52,723\nHe's gone,\nbut I'm moving forward.\n\n352\n00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:54,642\nT'Challa is dead,\n\n353\n00:23:54,725 --> 00:23:57,603\nbut that doesn't mean\nhe is gone.\n\n354\n00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,981\nWhen that illness\ntook your brother from us,\n\n355\n00:24:01,148 --> 00:24:05,653\nI had to lead a wounded nation\nand a broken world.\n\n356\n00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:08,530\nBut I still took time\nin the bush.\n\n357\n00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:11,951\nI wandered\nuntil I found water.\n\n358\n00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:13,494\nAnd I sat.\n\n359\n00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:16,789\nThen I did this ritual\n\n360\n00:24:16,956 --> 00:24:19,333\nthat I am about\nto show you now.\n\n361\n00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:21,835\n(SPIRITUAL MUSIC PLAYING)\n\n362\n00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:26,131\nI found your brother\nin the breeze,\n\n363\n00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:30,803\npushing me gently, but firm.\n\n364\n00:24:31,804 --> 00:24:33,973\nLike his hand on my shoulder.\n\n365\n00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:37,810\nIt took some time,\n\n366\n00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:41,146\nbut he was there.\n\n367\n00:24:47,361 --> 00:24:48,779\nHe wasn't there, Mother.\n\n368\n00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:52,032\nThe presence that you felt\n\n369\n00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:54,034\nwas just a construct\nof your mind.\n\n370\n00:24:54,118 --> 00:24:56,161\n(SPIRITUAL MUSIC CONTINUES)\n\n371\n00:24:56,245 --> 00:24:59,999\nBrought on so you could feel\nsome comfort or joy.\n\n372\n00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:02,126\nThat's all.\n\n373\n00:25:03,711 --> 00:25:04,878\nHmm.\n\n374\n00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:11,885\nWhat construct\ndoes your mind create\n\n375\n00:25:12,052 --> 00:25:14,013\nwhen you think\nof your brother?\n\n376\n00:25:14,972 --> 00:25:16,932\nDoes it offer you comfort?\n\n377\n00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,685\nOr torment?\n\n378\n00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:23,480\n(SPIRITUAL MUSIC CONTINUES)\n\n379\n00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:30,821\n(SIGHS)\n\n380\n00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,450\nCome, child.\n\n381\n00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:47,212\nHow did you get this?\n\n382\n00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:48,505\nWhat does it matter?\n\n383\n00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:51,133\nWhat does this have to do\nwith your ritual?\n\n384\n00:25:52,301 --> 00:25:54,636\nRAMONDA: Burning\nof the funeral garments\n\n385\n00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:57,056\nmarks the end\nof the mourning period\n\n386\n00:25:57,222 --> 00:26:00,142\nand the beginning\nof a new relationship\n\n387\n00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:02,478\nwith our loved ones\nthat have passed on...\n\n388\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-26T23:27:51.979Z","ordinal":43,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_CJOv9CoGFxnPY9HLTZgghkoW","output":"Chunk ID: 88a9d7\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1348\nOutput:\n00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,563\nI'm not doing this, Mother.\n\n389\n00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:07,274\nIf I sit\n\n390\n00:26:07,441 --> 00:26:09,985\nand think about my brother\nfor too long,\n\n391\n00:26:11,487 --> 00:26:14,281\nit won't be these clothes\nI'll burn.\n\n392\n00:26:15,532 --> 00:26:17,076\nIt will be the world...\n\n393\n00:26:18,494 --> 00:26:20,037\nand everyone in it.\n\n394\n00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:22,372\n(SIGHS) Shuri...\n\n395\n00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:29,755\nShuri, there's something\nthat I need to tell you\n\n396\n00:26:30,339 --> 00:26:31,548\nabout your brother.\n\n397\n00:26:31,632 --> 00:26:34,093\n(ELEPHANTS TRUMPETING)\n\n398\n00:26:36,095 --> 00:26:37,096\nMother, wait!\n\n399\n00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:39,640\n-What are you doing?\n-(FOOTSTEPS RUMBLING)\n\n400\n00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:41,100\n(RAMONDA PANTING)\n\n401\n00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:42,226\n(RUMBLING FADES)\n\n402\n00:26:46,522 --> 00:26:48,524\n(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)\n\n403\n00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:54,321\n(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)\n\n404\n00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:06,333\nThis better not be\na part of your ritual.\n\n405\n00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:07,751\nIt isn't.\n\n406\n00:27:09,378 --> 00:27:11,046\nRAMONDA: Stop! Right there!\n\n407\n00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,550\nWho are you?\nAnd how did you get in here?\n\n408\n00:27:16,093 --> 00:27:17,594\nThis place is amazing.\n\n409\n00:27:18,512 --> 00:27:20,597\nThe air is pristine.\n\n410\n00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:23,058\nAnd the water...\n\n411\n00:27:24,601 --> 00:27:26,728\nMy mother told stories\nabout a place like this.\n\n412\n00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:30,232\nA protected land with people\nthat never have to leave.\n\n413\n00:27:30,399 --> 00:27:32,734\nThat never have to change\nwho they were.\n\n414\n00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:35,404\nWhat reason do you have\n\n415\n00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:37,281\nto reveal your secret\nto the world?\n\n416\n00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:40,325\nlam not a woman\nwho enjoys repeating herself.\n\n417\n00:27:40,492 --> 00:27:42,369\nWho are you?\n\n418\n00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:43,745\nMAN: I have many names.\n\n419\n00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:47,457\nMy people call me\nK'uk'ulkan...\n\n420\n00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:52,087\nbut my enemies call me Namor.\n\n421\n00:27:53,881 --> 00:27:56,425\nThe American military\ndetected vibranium\n\n422\n00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,093\nunder my nation's domain.\n\n423\n00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:02,639\nI was able to\nstop them from minin' it,\n\n424\n00:28:03,557 --> 00:28:04,850\nbut we need Wakanda's help\n\n425\n00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:06,685\nto prevent it\nfrom happenin' again.\n\n426\n00:28:07,811 --> 00:28:10,772\nThey use a machine designed\nby an American scientist.\n\n427\n00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:13,442\nVibranium only exists here.\n\n428\n00:28:13,609 --> 00:28:14,943\nIn Wakanda.\n\n429\n00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:16,486\nMother, he's covered in it.\n\n430\n00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:24,119\nYour son exposed the power\nof vibranium to the world.\n\n431\n00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:26,997\nIn response,\nother nations have begun\n\n432\n00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,498\nsearching the planet for it.\n\n433\n00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:32,085\nHis choice has compromised us.\n\n434\n00:28:32,878 --> 00:28:35,255\nI think Wakanda\ncould find the scientist\n\n435\n00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:36,632\nand bring them to me?\n\n436\n00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:41,386\nIt is only fair that Wakanda\nhelps to resolve our dilemma.\n\n437\n00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:44,014\nYou do not sneak\ninto my country\n\n438\n00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:46,808\nand tell me what is fair.\n\n439\n00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:51,355\nI have more soldiers than\nthis land has blades of grass.\n\n440\n00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:54,858\nAnd they have\nincomparable strength.\n\n441\n00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:58,487\nI would hate to come back\nunder different circumstances.\n\n442\n00:29:00,948 --> 00:29:01,949\n(INHALES SHARPLY)\n\n443\n00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:06,954\nWhen you have the scientist,\nblow into this,\n\n444\n00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,455\nplace it in the ocean.\n\n445\n00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,916\nI'll be there\nshortly afterwards.\n\n446\n00:29:14,461 --> 00:29:15,671\nFor your own sake,\n\n447\n00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:18,090\ndon't mention\nanything about me\n\n448\n00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:19,967\nto anyone outside of Wakanda.\n\n449\n00:29:28,684 --> 00:29:30,602\nDid you see the wings\non his ankles?\n\n450\n00:29:31,353 --> 00:29:33,355\n(RAMONDA BREATHING SHAKILY)\n\n451\n00:29:45,367 --> 00:29:46,910\n(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)\n\n452\n00:29:46,994 --> 00:29:48,203\nSHURI: How did he do that?\n\n453\n00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:50,580\nRAMONDA:\nWe must convene the Council.\n\n454\n00:29:52,666 --> 00:29:54,209\nOKOYE: Heaven Scrapers\nhad no evidence\n\n455\n00:29:54,293 --> 00:29:56,003\nof any activity at all.\n\n456\n00:29:58,088 --> 00:30:02,926\nOh, the river border\nhas been breached, huh?\n\n457\n00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,469\nIf my soldiers were present,\n\n458\n00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:07,097\nthis \"fish man\"\n\n459\n00:30:07,264 --> 00:30:09,099\nwould be bound before us\nas we speak.\n\n460\n00:30:09,182 --> 00:30:11,435\nIf your muscle brains\nwere present,\n\n461\n00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:12,894\nthey would still be there\n\n462\n00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:14,771\nchoking on their\nfuzzy adornments.\n\n463\n00:30:14,855 --> 00:30:16,106\nYou bald-headed demon...\n\n464\n00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:18,066\nShow some respect, you two.\n\n465\n00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:19,234\nM'BAKU: Respect?\n\n466\n00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:21,820\nThese men should be\nashamed to show their faces!\n\n467\n00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:22,988\nWatch your tone, Jabari!\n\n468\n00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:25,157\n(JABARIS HOOTING)\n\n469\n00:30:26,992 --> 00:30:27,993\n"}}
